[3.054188, "o", "  1. handle_terminal_part gets the SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to LocalHistoryView.wheel.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[12;44H  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at; a hit on an agent viewport scrolls _HistoryViewport.offset and returns HistoryAction with\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[13;44H  render_history=True and forwarded_input=b\"\" — no upstream input.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[14;44H  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when action.forwarded_input is set; empty means nothing reaches tmux. The overlay is painted client-\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[15;44H  side via surface.paint_overlays.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[16;44H  4. This is a fast-client history overlay over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode; the implementation notes stock tmux WheelUpPane would enter\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[17;44H  copy-mode, which is deliberately avoided.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[18;44H  Focused test: tests/test_fast_full_window.py::test_local_history_routes_sidebar_immediately_and_owns_agent_wheel asserts\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[19;44H  agent_action.forwarded_input == b\"\".\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[20;44H  Suggested addition: assert agent_action.render_history is True, proving the overlay rendered rather than merely dropping the event.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[21;44H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\u001b[39;44H❯\u001b[39m \u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\u001b[40;44H────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────