[3.054569, "o", "\u001b[1;41r\u001b[1;44H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[1d\u001b[38;5;252m ▐▛███▜▌   Claude Code v2.1.220\u001b[2;44H▝▜█████▛▘  Opus 5 (1M context) · API Usage Billing\u001b[3;44H  ▘▘ ▝▝    /demo/railmux-web-workspace-v1/projects/railmux\u001b[5;44H\u001b[38;5;147m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252mIn railmux ssh, explain how a mouse-wheel event over an agent pane is served from the fast client's local history overlay rather than forwarded upstream. Point to\u001b[6;44H  the exact implementation symbols and one existing focused test that directly asserts empty forwarded_input. Then suggest one small additional assertion.\u001b[8;44H\u001b[38;5;147m●\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1mTrace SSH wheel ownership\u001b[9;44H  \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;252mrailmux ssh — agent-pane wheel served locally, not forwarded upstream:\u001b[10;44H  1. handle_terminal_part gets the SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to LocalHistoryView.wheel.\u001b[11;44H  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at; a hit on an agent viewport scrolls _HistoryViewport.offset and returns HistoryAction with render_history=True and\u001b[12;44H  forwarded_input=b\"\" — no upstream input.\u001b[13;44H  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when action.forwarded_input is set; empty means nothing reaches tmux. The overlay is painted client-side via\u001b[14;44H  surface.paint_overlays.\u001b[15;44H  4. This is a fast-client history overlay over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode; the implementation notes stock tmux WheelUpPane would enter copy-mode, which is\u001b[16;44H  deliberately avoided.\u001b[17;44H  Focused test: tests/test_fast_full_window.py::test_local_history_routes_sidebar_immediately_and_owns_agent_wheel asserts agent_action.forwarded_input == b\"\".\u001b[18;44H  Suggested addition: assert agent_action.render_history is True, proving the overlay rendered rather than merely dropping the event.\u001b[38;44H\u001b[38;5;239m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39;44H\u001b[38;5;147m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[40;44H\u001b[38;5;239m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[41;44H\u001b[38;5;244m  ⏵⏵ normal mode · shift+tab to cycle · ← for agents\u001b[1;42r\u001b[41;96H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
